Mission I: Paying great attention to execute flawless, stealthy infiltration;
Mission V: Starting to favour sharp stealth kills over sneaking past enemies and setting up accidents;
Mission IX: Developed interest in automatic weapons and killing hordes of alerted cops;
Mission XI: Murder everyone in sight exclusively with only a hammer whilst wearing a giant chipmunk suit.
The variety of ways in which missions can be accomplished is satisfactory.
On a slightly more serious note the story might be seen as a bit cliche and self-contradictory at times but it's also fitting agent 47 and brings you to some cool, beautiful places and situations. Controls can sometimes get a tad clumsy if you suddenly need to react fast but it shouldn't be an issue unless you want to go full on rambo through this stealth game which would be a waste considering the many elaborate & creative ways your targets can be killed without you ever being detected.
Player made contracts are a nice touch by adding more playtime to the game after the storyline is completed but after a dozen or so they start to feel too much like plain reshuffling of storyline missions.

