Tiny and Big is a fun short game.
Pros:
> Creativity on gameplay;
> Awsome music;
> Great art style;
> Funny characters and story.
Cons:
> Not very inspired level design: some tools, like the rocket, could be more explored (especially on the main objectives).
> The final boss fight is very difficult compared to the rest of the game. I think they should have prepared us more the boss fight mechanics.

A great game with the best FPS multiplayer I have ever played.
Its pros are:
A great multiplayer;
A very good story for the single player mode;
A few, but well defined classes for the multiplayer;
A good sort of weapons -again- for the multiplayer;
Good graphics.
The cons are:
The single player campaign is just too short;
Thare isn't a good variety of enemy skins in the single player;
Sometimes, in the single player campaign, you may find a few aleatory bugs;
The "Express 870 Shotgun" DLC, that turns the game into a sort of a "pay to win", but if you have it, you may find no problem (it is very cheap, so be sure to buy it when you buy the game).
Well, this game had bad times on Crytek's hands, but I think that now it will be back to where it should be, as it is being distributed by another company and is being sold again, here, on Steam.

This game doesn't feel right. The Story—North Koreans sucessfully invade and occupy the US of A—could be a wonderful setup for an excellent B-Movie style plot but personally I don't care much about any of the characters. At least the pilot guy I'm playing. The NPCs (the Goliath drone, too) just stand in the way, slow me down, won't let me open any door by myself and block the frame after kicking down the door, and so on and so on…
What I like:
• The graphics—not top notch anymore and probably never were, but the game looks cohesive in a good way;
• Beeing able to stand, crouch and prone is good—switching between crouching and standing is good for getting in and out of cover fast, and to prone helped me in some tough scenes;
• The setup of the story.
What I do not like:
• Guys, girls and drones standing in the way, blocking my view and blocking my way;
• Doors magically closing behind me;
• The weapons' sounds;
• Somehow I feel small in this game. The POV is like everyone is at least one head taller than "me".
• The story.
I've read the multiplayer-part of this game is decent, but beeing almost a pure single player I can't judge. For SPs like me I can not recommend this game.

